Error: Jet.ReadOnlyValueNotOwned: `greet` was not moved here, so it cannot be captured by a spawned task
  --> Tests/UI/task_detach_unsound.jet:5:13
    |
  5 |     t: task greet
    |             ^^^^^
 Why: This function can access the parameter, but it does not own the value; a capture here takes ownership
 Fix: Make the parameter owned: `greet: ^^fn()`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ReadOnlyValueNotOwned

Error: Jet.ValueNotSendable: This task returns `fn()`, which isn't sendable
  --> Tests/UI/task_detach_unsound.jet:5:13
    |
  5 |     t: task greet
    |             ^^^^^
 Why: The closure holds state that cannot cross this boundary; tasks and channels move owned values between threads
 Fix: Give the task plain owned data, or rebuild the value as an owned copy before spawning
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ValueNotSendable

Error: Jet.DetachUnsendableTask: Can't detach task `t` — it captured a value that can't cross a thread boundary
  --> Tests/UI/task_detach_unsound.jet:6:7
    |
  6 |     t.detach()
    |       ^^^^^^
 Why: A detached task runs unsupervised; it must only hold values it owns cleanly
 Fix: Fix the Jet.ValueNotSendable error at the spawn site first, then `.detach()` is safe
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.DetachUnsendableTask
